      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that it could just be a glitch but it feels too deliberate. like the flickering isnt random, it's like a pattern. and the thermostat stays on even when it's supposed to be dead. wouldn't advanced tech be able to use low frequency light pulses or something to transmit data without the person knowing? it feels like there's something more going on than just a bad circuit.",
