    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you about the encryption and the hardware stuff, but wouldn't a massive tech company with all the resources in the world be able to build those modifications into the chips before they even ship them? like, if it was built into the hardware from the factory, you wouldn't even know it's there. it would just look like a normal glitch to anyone else. how would i even tell the difference between a normal software bug and a hidden communication protocol if it's designed to look like a bug?",
